1
00:00:01,003 --> 00:00:04,104
Tokenized funds still settle like paper.

2
00:00:04,379 --> 00:00:07,545
Units move in one system, cash in another,

3
00:00:07,859 --> 00:00:10,135
and someone reconciles the gap by hand.

4
00:00:11,363 --> 00:00:13,382
Privity fixes that, on Canton.

5
00:00:13,657 --> 00:00:17,235
Both legs of a fund trade
commit in one transaction,

6
00:00:17,484 --> 00:00:19,748
so units and cash can never separate.

7
00:00:20,023 --> 00:00:23,562
And each counterparty sees
only the parcel it's buying,

8
00:00:23,902 --> 00:00:25,392
never the other side's book.

9
00:00:26,656 --> 00:00:27,515
Here's the trade.

10
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:30,891
Alice sells Bob four hundred
of her thousand units.

11
00:00:31,192 --> 00:00:34,332
First she earmarks exactly that parcel,

12
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:37,244
and only the parcel is disclosed to Bob.

13
00:00:37,507 --> 00:00:39,770
Her remaining six hundred stay private.

14
00:00:40,045 --> 00:00:43,017
Then one transaction
moves the units to Bob,

15
00:00:43,344 --> 00:00:44,796
and the cash to Alice.

16
00:00:45,071 --> 00:00:46,857
Both legs, or neither.

17
00:00:48,346 --> 00:00:49,256
That's the story.

18
00:00:49,532 --> 00:00:54,189
This is the evidence: a real run, captured
from a Canton participant through

19
00:00:54,209 --> 00:00:58,264
the JSON Ledger API, and
clearly labelled as a replay.

20
00:00:59,409 --> 00:01:02,819
Four claims, each checked
on the ledger or by test.

21
00:01:03,069 --> 00:01:04,662
Settlement is atomic.

22
00:01:04,924 --> 00:01:06,582
Disclosure is calibrated.

23
00:01:06,844 --> 00:01:09,185
A failed leg settles nothing.

24
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,626
And the NAV is checkable, not just signed.

25
00:01:13,763 --> 00:01:17,831
The timeline is the run
itself, with real update ids.

26
00:01:18,093 --> 00:01:20,730
The seller earmarks four hundred units,

27
00:01:20,864 --> 00:01:25,354
visible to the buyer, while the
retained six hundred are visible to the

28
00:01:25,374 --> 00:01:26,542
seller only.

29
00:01:26,817 --> 00:01:30,833
Then, delivery versus payment,
in a single transaction.

30
00:01:31,889 --> 00:01:32,606
Here it is.

31
00:01:32,868 --> 00:01:36,369
The seller signed the proposal,
and the buyer exercises it,

32
00:01:36,477 --> 00:01:39,526
so one transaction
carries both authorities.

33
00:01:39,801 --> 00:01:40,931
Shares transfer.

34
00:01:41,206 --> 00:01:43,688
Cash splits, and pays the seller.

35
00:01:43,951 --> 00:01:45,299
Eight events, one commit.

36
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:48,690
Now the part a public chain can't do.

37
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:51,049
Each row is an active contract query,

38
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:52,995
issued as that party.

39
00:01:53,257 --> 00:01:55,907
The buyer sees its parcel and its cash,

40
00:01:56,169 --> 00:01:58,626
and cannot see the
seller's remaining units.

41
00:01:58,901 --> 00:02:03,124
The auditor sees only its
mandate and the NAV attestation.

42
00:02:03,399 --> 00:02:05,508
And the privacy check passes.

43
00:02:06,837 --> 00:02:08,791
Under the hood, it's plain Daml.

44
00:02:09,054 --> 00:02:12,400
Settlement is one choice,
controlled by the buyer.

45
00:02:12,662 --> 00:02:14,964
It checks the parcel is earmarked to them,

46
00:02:15,239 --> 00:02:17,258
and that their cash covers the price.

47
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:20,866
Then it runs the delivery leg
and the payment leg together.

48
00:02:21,129 --> 00:02:23,701
If any check fails, nothing commits.

49
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:26,416
NAV works the same way.

50
00:02:26,679 --> 00:02:32,177
The ledger commits to the book with a
sha256 hash over the sorted holdings.

51
00:02:32,439 --> 00:02:37,228
An entitled auditor recomputes
it, and the attestation verifies.

52
00:02:37,503 --> 00:02:39,561
Change one unit, and it doesn't.

53
00:02:39,823 --> 00:02:41,867
An investor can't run the check at all.

54
00:02:43,203 --> 00:02:44,848
And you don't need to trust the page.

55
00:02:45,136 --> 00:02:48,791
One command runs the whole
flow on your own participant,

56
00:02:48,912 --> 00:02:51,472
and prints a receipt: the transaction,

57
00:02:51,579 --> 00:02:55,802
digest and NAV verification,
the privacy verdict,

58
00:02:55,871 --> 00:02:57,245
and the saved artifact.

59
00:02:57,494 --> 00:03:00,750
It exits zero only if everything passes.

60
00:03:02,483 --> 00:03:03,033
Privity.

61
00:03:03,346 --> 00:03:06,164
Fund trades that cannot half-settle,

62
00:03:06,413 --> 00:03:08,960
with disclosure calibrated
to need to know.

63
00:03:09,249 --> 00:03:12,285
Built on Canton, for
HackCanton Season Three.
